cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the accompanying manuscript, please cite it as below."
title: "SDF-Lattice NGC 6503: radial-unfreezing closure, verification code and audit record"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and audit record for the radial-unfreezing closure of
  the Spacetime Dielectric Foam (SDF / QVEX) framework, applied to the SPARC
  rotation curve of the dwarf spiral galaxy NGC 6503. The canonical closure is
  v_model^2 = v_bar^2 + (v_inf^2 - v_bar^2) * zeta(r) with
  zeta(r) = 0.5 * (1 + tanh((r - R0) / DeltaR)); v_inf is the total asymptotic
  circular speed, an observable, not an additive model component. On the 31-bin
  SPARC table the adopted parameters give chi^2 = 39.607 with N = 31 and p = 1,
  i.e. chi^2_nu = 1.320, which fails the project's own < 1.25 target; fitting the
  transition with the stellar mass-to-light ratio pinned at 0.5 gives 1.190, and
  leaving it free drives Upsilon_disk to its lower bound of 0.01. Earlier values
  of 0.942 and 2.716 are withdrawn and documented as such. The repository
  includes the verbatim SPARC data file, its provenance and checksum, a
  standard-library-only verification script, a citation-coverage checker, and
  the manuscript sources.
